      "purpose": "A utility program (CRTFRMSTMF) that creates an IBM i object from a source file stored in the IFS stream file system. It accepts an object name, a create command (e.g. CRTBNDCL, CRTPF, CRTSRVPGM), a stream file path, and optional parameters. It copies the IFS source into a temporary source physical file (QTEMP/QSOURCE) via CPYFRMSTMF, then invokes the appropriate CRT* command via QCAPCMD (ProcessCommand API), sending an escape message on failure. Uses QCMDEXC, QCAPCMD, and QMHSNDPM IBM i system APIs.",
